    {
      "id": "a55f56db-098c-441c-ac0f-3ef296e75efa",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview & setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -848,
        -640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 1720,
        "content": "# Triage Gmail emails with Jev decisions and draft replies with OpenAI\n\n\n[![VIDEO](https://img.youtube.com/vi/1HFTuRrkr2k/maxresdefault.jpg)](https://youtu.be/1HFTuRrkr2k)\n\n# \ud83d\udce5  [Open full documentation on Notion](https://automatisation.notion.site/n8n-Jev-sort-and-answer-your-Gmail-emails-with-an-AI-that-decides-3f33d6550fd981a3ae7df36d80348c0f)\n\n**Canvas map**\n1. Receive and prepare the email\n2. Let Jev decide (System One)\n3. Apply the Gmail label\n4. Draft a reply when one is needed\n5. Log every decision\n\n## How it works\nEvery new email is sent to **Jev**, TypeSafe AI's System One model. Jev does not write text: it returns calibrated probabilities on options you define.\n- **Evaluate** asks 3 typed questions in one call: urgency (score 0-3), needs a reply (yes/no probability), upset customer (yes/no probability).\n- **Route** picks the team (Sales, Support, Billing, Partnerships, Newsletters, Spam) and replaces a Switch node. When Jev is less sure than `route_confidence_threshold`, the email leaves from **Fallback** and gets the `Jev/To review` label for a human.\n- Only emails that need a reply (and are not Spam or Newsletters) reach the LLM, which writes a **Gmail draft** in the same thread. Nothing is ever sent automatically.\n- Every decision is stored in a Data Table so you can measure accuracy, volume and cost.\n\nJev is the fast, cheap decision step (System 1). The LLM only runs on the few emails that need words (System 2).\n\n## Setup\n1. Install the community node `@typesafe-ai/n8n-nodes-typesafe-ai` (Settings > Community nodes). On n8n Cloud, Jev is already available.\n2. Create a **TypeSafe AI API** credential with your key from console.typesafe.ai and select it on the 2 Jev nodes.\n3. Connect Gmail (OAuth2) and OpenAI credentials.\n4. In Gmail, create the labels `Jev/Sales`, `Jev/Support`, `Jev/Billing`, `Jev/Partnerships`, `Jev/Newsletters`, `Jev/Spam`, `Jev/To review`, then pick one in each **Label as ...** node.\n5. Create a Data Table with the columns used by **Log Jev decision** and select it.\n6. Edit **Configuration**, then activate.\n\n## Requirements\n- n8n self-hosted with the TypeSafe AI community node, or n8n Cloud\n- TypeSafe AI API key (Jev)\n- Gmail account (OAuth2)\n- OpenAI API key\n\nSelf-hosted tip: if installing the node fails with \"Class could not be found\", the `n8n-workflow` package in `~/.n8n/nodes` is outdated. Run `npm install n8n-workflow@<your n8n version> --ignore-scripts` in that folder and restart n8n.\n\n## Customization\n- Change the teams in **Route email to department** (names become outputs) and add one label node per new output.\n- Raise `route_confidence_threshold` to send more emails to human review, lower it to automate more.\n- Replace the Gmail draft with a Slack or Telegram alert for Critical urgency.\n\nJev can still pick the wrong option: the confidence gate and the draft-only replies keep a human in the loop.\n\nNeed help customizing?\nContact me for consulting and support : [Linkedin](https://www.linkedin.com/in/doctor-firass/)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
